<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#rice-terrace">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rice terrace</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as terraced paddies</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> terrace is a series of stepped, levelled fields cut into hillsides to allow the irrigated cultivation of rice on sloping ground. Terracing conserves water and soil and makes intensive farming possible in upland areas. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit Empire</a> profile notes that terraced paddies in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> supported dense populations and produced the surplus on which taxation and tribute depended.</p></div>
